# WordPress Localization (i18n)

This project uses localization. Text domain: `mksddn-reddy-auth`.

## When Adding or Changing User-Facing Text

- Wrap every user-visible string in i18n helpers: `__()`, `_e()`, `esc_html__()`, `esc_attr__()`, `_n()`, `_x()` as appropriate.
- Never hardcode UI labels, errors, or admin descriptions in PHP without i18n wrappers.
- Use escaped translation helpers at render time (`esc_html__`, `esc_attr__`).

## Translation Files

- Catalogs live in `mksddn-reddy-auth/trunk/languages/`.
- When adding new `msgid` strings, update **both**:
  - `mksddn-reddy-auth-en_US.po`
  - `mksddn-reddy-auth-ru_RU.po` (with Russian `msgstr`)
- Keep entries alphabetically sorted by `msgid` when practical.
- Recompile `.mo` files when `msgfmt` is available.

## Definition of Done (i18n)

A change is not complete until:

1. All new user-facing strings use the project text domain.
2. Matching entries exist in `.po` files for new strings.
3. Russian translations are provided in `mksddn-reddy-auth-ru_RU.po`.

## Examples

```php
// Admin field label
__( 'Allowed Reddy IDs', 'mksddn-reddy-auth' );

// Rendered description
esc_html__( 'One Reddy ID per line. Empty = no restriction.', 'mksddn-reddy-auth' );

// REST/user error (neutral message)
__( 'Unable to process authentication request.', 'mksddn-reddy-auth' );
```
